This project contains raw data, including full read information, as well as Seurat objects associated with the [paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-021-04358-6) **"Autism genes converge on asynchronous development of shared neuron classes"**, as well as the upcoming paper associated with the [study](https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2022.03.17.484798v1) **"Single-cell multiomics atlas of organoid development uncovers longitudinal molecular programs of cellular diversification of the human cerebral cortex"**. These works came out of a collaboration between the labs of Paola Arlotta, Aviv Regev, and Joshua Levin. 

