#Crab-eating Macaque Brain RNA editing
####Adenosine-to-inosine (A-I) RNA editing represents one of the most abundant post-transcriptional RNA modification processes within the mammalian central nervous system. However, the lack of a precise and comprehensive inventory of RNA editing in non-human primate (NHP) brains hampers the exploration of A-I RNA editing in understanding the mammalian brain’s evolution and function. Here, we performed whole-genome and whole-transcriptome sequencing to identify 2,782,079 A-I editing sites in 39 anatomically defined brain regions of adult Macaca fascicularis (crab-eating macaque). 
